From 01788a16c4796b2f3db55d67e29365100a5f3c0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): completing a card no longer voids its
 filed supervisor request
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A worker that files an operator comment for another gateway's card and then
completes (a comment is naturally a worker's last act) lost the comment: the
executor ran a few seconds later and `requester_refusal` rejected the request
with "requester <id> is done". Two cross-gateway comments were lost this way
in 24 h (t_01a1cfe6aecb13cf on worker-2, t_01a1cfcee4684ee2 on worker-1).

The rule came from the park-and-wait graph-edit design (3d043a9abb); the
operator call inherited it when it reused the request path (f1b1c8eb70).

- `requester_refusal` refuses only a missing or archived requester. A `done`
  requester's queued request executes; `submit` already required a live
  dispatcher run, and every executor still re-checks the op's scope against
  the board as it is now. Archiving stays the cancel signal.
- The operator call forwards `requested_at` = the request's `created_at`
  (submit time), not the forwarding tick. The home proves the caller's run was
  live at `requested_at` (±120 s); with the tick time a dispatcher that ran
  more than 120 s after the caller completed would still lose the comment as
  `caller_unproven`.
- Tool text: "Completing this card does not cancel a filed request (archiving
  it does); park only if you need the result."
- retry_limit: its docstring and test pinned "a finished requester is
  refused"; per the decided fix it now applies, and a new test pins that an
  archived requester is still rejected.

Proof:
- New tests: test_operator_comment_lands_after_requester_completes (fleet,
  comment lands once, request done with no error, supervisor_request_done
  receipt on the caller, caller stays done),
  test_late_forward_after_completion_is_proven_at_submit_time,
  test_unlink_applies_after_requester_completes,
  test_requester_finished_before_execute_still_applies (retry_limit),
  test_requester_archived_before_execute_is_rejected (retry_limit).
- RED on origin/main source: exactly the three new operator/supervisor tests
  fail; the other 54 in those files pass (incl.
  test_archived_requester_is_rejected_at_execution and
  test_evicted_caller_copy_still_finishes).
- GREEN: test_kanban_operator_call.py 31/31 (29 + 2),
  test_kanban_supervisor_requests.py 26/26 (25 + 1); all 29 test files that
  import the touched modules: 727 passed, 0 failed.
- Mutants: reverting requested_at to the tick time fails only the
  late-forward test; dropping the archived refusal fails 3 supervisor tests.
